# Search exclusions (ripgrep — what Claude Code's Grep and Glob run on).
#
# These trees are generated: nothing here is ours to change, and a fix applied
# inside one is reverted by the next `init.py` refresh out of the installed
# plugin. `pyproject.toml` already excludes the same paths from ruff and mypy
# for exactly that reason — this is the third tool that should not read them.
#
# `vendor/` and `.claude/skills/skill-creator/references/` were here too until
# T58: upstream is installed from the marketplace now, so neither the subtree
# nor the vendored arsenal skills exist in this working tree at all. Nothing
# under `~/.claude/plugins/` is reachable from a repository-relative search, so
# it needs no exclusion.
#
# `!` re-includes a path. Search a generated tree deliberately with
# `rg --no-ignore-vcs -u` or by naming its directory as the search path.

claude-arsenal/bin/
claude-arsenal/scripts/

# Generated readers — the committed HTML/annotated copies of specs that live in
# source form elsewhere. Matching both means every spec hit is reported twice.
docs/spec-v2/spec-reader.html
docs/spec-v2-steps/spec-reader.html

# Caches and build output.
.venv/
__pycache__/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
dist/
